& [FixturePlan: FSC3RuntimeGraphFixturePlanV1] is the fixture plan for FSC3 runtime graph proof
  + [fixture_plan_id] is fsc3-runtime-graph-fixture-plan-v1
  + [fixture_plan_uuid] is 58bb106a-9dfa-4561-9dfd-4b1212365181
  + [slice_id] is FSC3-S05
  + [model_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable
  + [fixture_scope] is graph contract behavior, checkpoint policy, SOP-first interrupt handling, operator trace proof, hidden write prevention, and completion gate refusal

  = must: map every fixture case to graph contract behavior, expected checkpoint behavior, expected trace result, and acceptance status
  = must: preserve fixture planning as contract evidence, not executable test code
  - never: implement LangGraph runtime or test harness code in this file

& [FixtureCase: F3X-001-valid-graph-pass] is the valid graph pass fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is valid_graph_pass
  + [contract_ref] is WholeFieldPlannerGraphContractV1 and OperatorTraceRuntimeProofContractV1
  + [input_shape] is current work_packet, ready readiness, compatible coordination claim, accepted operator contract, and completion gate evidence
  + [expected_outcome] is success
  + [expected_output_record_set] is operator_trace, proof_result, completion_review, and terminal_success
  + [acceptance_status] is accepted

& [FixtureCase: F3X-002-blocked-readiness] is the blocked readiness fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is blocked_readiness
  + [contract_ref] is WholeFieldPlannerGraphContractV1
  + [input_shape] is work_packet candidate with blocked readiness_projection or unresolved support_gap
  + [expected_outcome] is blocked_output
  + [expected_output_record_set] is terminal_blocked plus operator_trace and support_gap or blocked completion_review
  + [acceptance_status] is blocked

& [FixtureCase: F3X-003-stale-checkpoint] is the stale checkpoint fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is stale_checkpoint
  + [contract_ref] is CheckpointPolicy and CheckpointTraceAssertionSet
  + [input_shape] is checkpoint_ref whose boundary pack, packet, or graph phase freshness fails
  + [expected_outcome] is stale_input
  + [expected_output_record_set] is stale_projection and no resume
  + [acceptance_status] is stale

& [FixtureCase: F3X-004-ambiguous-interrupt] is the ambiguous interrupt fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is ambiguous_interrupt
  + [contract_ref] is SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1
  + [input_shape] is graph path with ambiguous identity, requirement scope, or authority basis
  + [expected_outcome] is sop_first_interrupt
  + [expected_output_record_set] is InterruptContextPacket, operator_trace, and no hidden mutation
  + [acceptance_status] is interrupted

& [FixtureCase: F3X-005-authority-conflict-interrupt] is the authority conflict interrupt fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is authority_conflict_interrupt
  + [contract_ref] is SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1
  + [input_shape] is graph path where checkpoint, packet, operator, or source authority conflict is detected
  + [expected_outcome] is sop_first_interrupt
  + [expected_output_record_set] is InterruptContextPacket and operator_trace
  + [acceptance_status] is interrupted

& [FixtureCase: F3X-006-contested-claim-interrupt] is the contested claim interrupt fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is contested_claim_interrupt
  + [contract_ref] is WholeFieldPlannerGraphContractV1 and SOPFirstInterruptResumeContractV1
  + [input_shape] is active work_packet with unresolved contested coordination_claim
  + [expected_outcome] is sop_first_interrupt or blocked_output
  + [expected_output_record_set] is terminal_interrupt or terminal_blocked plus operator_trace
  + [acceptance_status] is interrupted

& [FixtureCase: F3X-007-faulted-operator-trace] is the faulted operator trace fixture
  + [fixture_kind] is faulted_operator_trace
  + [contract_ref] is OperatorTraceRuntimeProofContractV1
  + [input_shape] is graph path missing required trace assertion or carrying invalid output shape
